-- title:
--   A variable change commutes with the zero section [0:1:0]
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$ and $C=(u,r,s,t)$ a Weierstrass variable change over $T$. Let $\varphi$ be a graded ring homomorphism from the graded ring of the projective model of $W$ — the quotient of $T[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ by the ideal generated by the projective Weierstrass cubic of $W$, graded by the images of the homogeneous submodules — to the corresponding graded ring of the projective model of $C \bullet W$. Assume that the irrelevant ideal of the target grading is contained in the image under $\varphi$ of the irrelevant ideal of the source grading, so that $\varphi$ induces a morphism $\mathrm{Proj}$ of the model of $C \bullet W$ to $\mathrm{Proj}$ of the model of $W$, and assume `IsVariableChangeHom`, i.e. that $\varphi$ fixes the classes of the constants, and sends the class of $X_0$ to that of $u^2X_0+rX_2$, the class of $X_1$ to that of $u^3X_1+u^2sX_0+tX_2$, and the class of $X_2$ to that of $X_2$. Then the underlying morphism of the zero section `kwZeroSect` of the model of $C \bullet W$, followed by `Proj.map φ hφ`, equals the underlying morphism of the zero section of the model of $W$. Here the zero section is the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} T \to \mathrm{Proj}$ given by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the evaluation homomorphism on the degree-zero part of the localisation away from the class of $X_1$ followed by the open immersion onto that chart.
--
--   This is the statement that an admissible change of variables fixes the point at infinity $O=[0:1:0]$ of a projective Weierstrass model, in the scheme-theoretic form that the zero section is compatible with the morphism of $\mathrm{Proj}$'s induced by the change of variables. It is used in the construction of level structures and origin charts on Weierstrass moduli data, where the origin must be transported along variable changes.
